module TokenDisbursement where

-- LoanStatus
--   Typed status replaces the previous status : Text field. Using an ADT
--   means a typo like "Approvd" no longer compiles, and pattern matching
--   on status is exhaustive-checked by the compiler.
data LoanStatus = Approved | Rejected
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- 1. TokenWallet Template
--
-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Represents an account-based token wallet that holds a borrower's
--   disbursed loan balance. The issuer credits funds on disbursement;
--   the owner debits funds when spending or repaying. The separation of
--   credit (issuer-controlled) and debit (owner-controlled) mirrors the
--   real-world model where a bank deposits funds into a customer account
--   and the customer controls outgoing transactions.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: issuer, owner
--   Both parties co-sign the wallet because it represents a custodial
--   relationship — the issuer holds and manages the funds, the owner
--   has the right to the balance. Dual signatories prevent either party
--   from unilaterally creating or closing the account.
--
-- OBSERVERS: none
--   No third-party observers. The wallet balance is private to the
--   account holder and the issuing institution.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   GDPR Article 5(1)(c) — data minimization. The wallet is visible only
--   to issuer and owner; no other party can observe the borrower's balance.
--   CFPB Regulation Z — the issuer-controlled Credit choice ensures funds
--   can only be added by the lending institution as part of an approved
--   disbursement, not self-credited by the borrower.
template TokenWallet
  with
    owner : Party
    issuer : Party
    tokenAmount : Decimal
  where
    signatory issuer, owner

    choice Credit : ContractId TokenWallet
      with
        amount : Decimal
      controller issuer
        do
          assertMsg "The amount should be positive" (amount > 0.0)
          create this with
            tokenAmount = tokenAmount + amount

    choice Debit : ContractId TokenWallet
      with
        amount : Decimal
      controller owner
        do
          assertMsg "Insufficient balance" (amount <= tokenAmount)
          assertMsg "Sent amount should be greater than zero" (amount > 0.0)
          create this with
            tokenAmount = tokenAmount - amount

-- 2. LoanLimit Template
--
-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Represents the bank's credit concentration control — a bank-wide
--   lending capacity that decrements with each approved loan and tracks
--   how much the institution can still lend across all active borrowers.
--   This is distinct from the per-borrower limit governed by 12 USC 84
--   (OCC legal lending limit, capped at 15% of unimpaired capital per
--   single borrower). The totalLimit here models an aggregate portfolio
--   constraint: the bank has a total pool of lendable funds, and each
--   approval draws from that pool until it is exhausted.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: issuer
--   The bank is the sole signatory because lending capacity is an
--   institutional asset that the bank alone controls.
--
-- OBSERVERS: none
--   The bank's total lending capacity and internal limits are
--   proprietary credit risk data and not visible to borrowers.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   FDIC Interagency Guidelines for Credit Concentration Risk — the
--   totalLimit field implements a portfolio-level concentration control.
--   12 USC 84 (OCC Legal Lending Limit) — acknowledged as the statutory
--   per-borrower cap; the totalLimit here models the bank's internal
--   aggregate capacity, a complementary but distinct control.
template LoanLimit
  with
    issuer : Party
    loanLimit : Decimal
    loanRequested : Decimal
    totalLimit : Decimal
  where
    signatory issuer

    choice CheckLimit : ContractId LoanLimit
      with
        loanAmount : Decimal
        salary : Decimal
      controller issuer
        do
          assertMsg "Loan must be within 25% of the salary"
            (loanAmount <= 0.25 * salary)
          assertMsg "Loan Limit Exceeded" (loanAmount <= totalLimit)
          create this with
            loanLimit = 0.25 * salary
            totalLimit = totalLimit - loanAmount
            loanRequested = loanAmount

-- 3. LoanRequest Template
--
-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Extends the basic loan application from Module 1 with income-based
--   eligibility verification and integration with the bank's lending
--   capacity limit. The borrower provides their salary alongside the
--   requested amount. ApproveRequest asserts the 25% DTI rule and
--   exercises CheckLimit on the LoanLimit contract; a request that fails
--   either check aborts the transaction. Explicit rejections (for any
--   non-DTI reason) go through RejectRequest, which produces an audit
--   record without consuming lending capacity.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: owner (borrower)
--   The borrower signs the request, committing their stated income and
--   requested amount to the ledger. This creates an on-ledger record
--   of the borrower's representations at time of application, which
--   supports the bank's documentation obligation under BSA CIP rules.
--
-- OBSERVERS: issuer (bank)
--   The bank observes the request to evaluate and exercise the approval
--   choice. It does not co-sign the request because it has not yet made
--   a credit decision.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   CFPB Ability-to-Repay (Regulation Z) — the 25% debt-to-income check
--   inside ApproveRequest enforces income-based lending eligibility as a
--   contract assertion. A failing request cannot produce an Approved loan.
--   BSA Section 1020.220 (Customer Identification Program) — the owner
--   party represents the identified loan applicant.
template LoanRequest
  with
    loanLimitCid : ContractId LoanLimit
    issuer : Party
    owner : Party
    salary : Decimal
    loanAmount : Decimal
  where
    ensure loanAmount > 0.0 && salary > 0.0
    signatory owner
    observer issuer

    choice ApproveRequest : ContractId Loan
      controller issuer
      do
        assertMsg "Loan exceeds 25% of stated salary (CFPB Ability-to-Repay)"
          (loanAmount <= 0.25 * salary)
        _ <- exercise loanLimitCid CheckLimit with
          salary = salary
          loanAmount = loanAmount
        create Loan with
          issuer
          owner
          loanAmount
          disbursedAmount = 0.0
          status = Approved

    choice RejectRequest : ContractId Loan
      controller issuer
      do
        create Loan with
          issuer
          owner
          loanAmount
          disbursedAmount = 0.0
          status = Rejected

-- 4. Loan Template
--
-- FINANCIAL CONTEXT:
--   Extends the Module 1 Loan contract with disbursement tracking.
--   Adds disbursedAmount to record how much of the approved loan has
--   been released into the borrower's wallet. The Disburse choice allows
--   the bank to release funds incrementally — each tranche is validated
--   against the approved loanAmount before the Credit choice on the
--   TokenWallet is exercised.
--
-- SIGNATORIES: issuer, owner
--   Both parties co-sign the loan agreement.
--
-- OBSERVERS: none
--   Loan terms and disbursement status are private to the contracting parties.
--
-- COMPLIANCE:
--   CFPB Regulation Z — the Disburse choice assertion
--   (disbursedAmount + disAmount <= loanAmount) enforces that total
--   disbursement never exceeds the approved credit limit.
--   FDIC Credit Concentration Guidelines — the disbursedAmount field
--   provides on-ledger visibility into actual funds released.
template Loan
  with
    issuer : Party
    owner : Party
    loanAmount : Decimal
    disbursedAmount : Decimal
    status : LoanStatus
  where
    signatory issuer, owner

    choice Disburse : ContractId Loan
      with
        disAmount : Decimal
        tokenWalletCid : ContractId TokenWallet
      controller issuer
      do
        assertMsg "Disbursement Amount must be positive" (disAmount > 0.0)
        assertMsg "Disbursement exceeds remaining limit"
          (disbursedAmount + disAmount <= loanAmount)
        _ <- exercise tokenWalletCid Credit with amount = disAmount
        create this with
          disbursedAmount = disbursedAmount + disAmount
